Tue Nov 10 07:28:29 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 0.3.5:
  * Linux Intel GPU (i915/xe) support is now upstream, including
    GT clock, throttle status, private iGPU memory accounting and
    a CPU-package temperature fallback: drop
    gputaskman-intel-i915-xe.patch.
  * New system RAM/CPU panel with per-process RAM/CPU columns and
    a 'gputaskman record' command for append-only JSON snapshots.
  * More reliable identity: exact-LUID Windows ROOT display
    adapter names, vLLM model IDs with parent API provenance, and
    snapshot diffs rejecting different adapters and reused PIDs.
  * Safer model inspection: deduplicated GGUF paths, null-safe
    Ollama manifests, authenticated local llama-server probes.
  * WSL2 NVML discovery in Nix, no NVML sweep on non-NVIDIA GPUs.

